  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A mass–spring system oscillates with time period <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"T_{1}\"></span>.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>Another identical spring is connected in parallel with the first spring as shown. The mass is unchanged.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_02\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 2\" src=\"asset:fig_02\"/></figure></p>\n<p>The time period of the oscillation for the two-spring system is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"T_{2}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>What is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{T_{2}}{T_{1}}\"></span>?</p>\n<p>[1]</p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{2}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\sqrt{2}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2\"></span></li></ol>"
  },
